1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,965
Torpedo hole. Discovered by

2
00:00:03,005 --> 00:00:05,382
government divers in the Maine.

3
00:00:05,422 --> 00:00:07,799
A New York front page, two days

4
00:00:07,839 --> 00:00:10,215
after the battleship Maine blew

5
00:00:10,255 --> 00:00:11,869
up in Havana.

6
00:00:12,919 --> 00:00:15,224
Divers found an eight inch hole

7
00:00:15,264 --> 00:00:17,493
in her plates, the paper said.

8
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:18,930
Proof of a torpedo.

9
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:20,931
Spanish treachery.

10
00:00:21,981 --> 00:00:24,045
But look lower, on the same

11
00:00:24,085 --> 00:00:26,460
front page. Divers will go down

12
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,581
today at the wreck.

13
00:00:29,931 --> 00:00:31,988
The Navy's divers reached Havana

14
00:00:32,028 --> 00:00:32,971
two days later.

15
00:00:33,011 --> 00:00:35,642
The paper never named a source.

16
00:00:38,131 --> 00:00:40,464
Ten weeks later, America and

17
00:00:40,504 --> 00:00:41,989
Spain were at war.

18
00:00:42,029 --> 00:00:44,532
In March, the Navy's court had

19
00:00:44,572 --> 00:00:47,244
found a mine, but no evidence of

20
00:00:47,284 --> 00:00:48,223
who.

21
00:00:48,973 --> 00:00:51,393
In nineteen seventy six, a Navy

22
00:00:51,433 --> 00:00:53,933
study said: there is no evidence

23
00:00:53,973 --> 00:00:56,473
